# Packages required for interactive AOMP development that the TheRock
# manylinux base image (AlmaLinux 8.10) does not already provide.
#
# The base recipe (build_manylinux_x86_64.Dockerfile) deliberately installs
# development *tools* (cmake, ninja, ccache, gcc-toolset-13, git, python,
# googletest, rust) but NOT development *packages*, so that portable release
# builds cannot accidentally link against system libraries. That guardrail is
# for the CI/CD release images. This is a local development image, where we
# want the headers present so AOMP just builds; the -devel packages below are
# an intentional relaxation of that rule, not a mistake to be "cleaned up".
#
# Only packages confirmed missing from a running base image are listed here.
# Tools already pinned by the base (cmake, ninja, ccache, gcc/g++/gfortran,
# git, git-lfs, python, gtest, rust, libtool, patchelf, make, curl, gdb) are
# intentionally omitted so they are not shadowed by older dnf variants.
#
# AOMP build dependencies (development libraries)
elfutils-devel
elfutils-libelf-devel
expat-devel
fmt-devel
gmp-devel
libatomic
libbabeltrace-devel
libffi-devel
libquadmath-devel
mpfr-devel
msgpack-devel
ncurses-devel
numactl-devel
ocl-icd-devel
openssl-devel
pciutils-devel
sqlite-devel
systemd-devel
xz-devel
# Packaging/util support used by the AOMP build scripts
rpm-build
# Interactive development utilities missing from the base
rsync
vim-enhanced
wget
